From: rhythmcache <153998419+rhythmcache@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] selinux: fix reset_avc_cache() on < 5.10 kernels

c70c71761 ("kernel: Fix SELinux generation tracking for policy updates")
changed reset_avc_cache() to take a seqno and replaced the pre-5.10 call
sites with reset_avc_cache(pol->latest_granting). On 5.4, struct
selinux_policy is not defined and pol is not available in the pre-5.10
branches, so the build fails with:

  kernel/selinux/rules.c:261:24: error: incomplete definition of type 'struct selinux_policy'
  kernel/selinux/rules.c:782:21: error: use of undeclared identifier 'pol'

Use reset_avc_cache(0) in the pre-5.10 paths, matching the old
reset_avc_cache(void) behavior which hardcoded seqno 0.

Fixes: c70c71761 ("kernel: Fix SELinux generation tracking for policy updates (tiann/KernelSU#3964)")
Signed-off-by: rhythmcache <153998419+rhythmcache@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 kernel/selinux/rules.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/selinux/rules.c b/kernel/selinux/rules.c
index 85c8b301b..e8194230e 100644
--- a/kernel/selinux/rules.c
+++ b/kernel/selinux/rules.c
@@ -258,7 +258,7 @@ do_stop_machine:
 
 out_flush:
     smp_mb();
-    reset_avc_cache(pol->latest_granting);
+    reset_avc_cache(0);
 #ifdef CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS
     susfs_set_batch_sid();
 #endif
@@ -779,7 +779,7 @@ out_done:
         goto out_free;
 
     smp_mb();
-    reset_avc_cache(pol->latest_granting);
+    reset_avc_cache(0);
     ret = success_cmd_count;
 
 out_free:
